# Spec-driven product repo

This repository was bootstrapped with **`spec/`** as the canonical place for
product requirements, backlog, and acceptance stories.

## Machine-readable specs

When **`spec/prd.spec.yaml`** and **`spec/stories.spec.yaml`** are present, agents
should prefer them for **id lists, traceability, and structured scenarios**, and use
markdown (`prd.md`, `stories.md`) for narrative review and stakeholder wording.

## Before coding

1. Read **`spec/digest.md`** for a short, current picture of scope and ids.
2. Use **Story ids** and **FR/NFR ids** from YAML or markdown consistently.
3. Follow **Epic → Feature → Story → Task** from `spec/task-breakdown.md` without renaming levels.

## Artifacts

- **`spec/prd.spec.yaml`** / **`spec/stories.spec.yaml`** — compact structured specs (see upstream `docs/spec-schema.md` in the RFP workflow repo if copied).
- **`spec/prd.md`** — full PRD (human review, detailed requirements).
- **`spec/architecture.md`** — solution architecture and stack decision (when copied).
- **`spec/stories.md`** — user stories and Gherkin for testing and delivery.
- **`spec/task-breakdown.md`** — implementation planning hierarchy.
- **`spec/clarifications.md`** — questions, assumptions, and clarification history.
- **`spec/planning-sheet.csv`** — planning / estimates export.
- **`spec/CHANGELOG.md`** — append-only log of spec changes (keep in sync when PRD shifts).

## Agent discipline

- Prefer **targeted excerpts** (by id or heading) over pasting entire files each turn.
- When the PRD or stories change, update **`spec/digest.md`** and append **`spec/CHANGELOG.md`**.
- Do not invent scope beyond **`spec/prd.md`** / **`spec/prd.spec.yaml`** without an explicit change request.
- For additive scope, use **`spec-add-requirement`** (`.cursor/skills/spec-add-requirement/SKILL.md` or `.claude/skills/spec-add-requirement/SKILL.md`) so markdown and YAML stay aligned.
- Follow **`docs/living-documentation.md`** for ongoing doc hygiene and **`docs/engineering-guidelines.md`** for stack guardrails (Cursor: also **`engineering-guardrails.mdc`**).

See **`AGENTS.md`** for cross-tool guidance. **Claude Code** loads **`CLAUDE.md`** and **`.claude/skills/`**; **GitHub Copilot** uses **`.github/copilot-instructions.md`** in addition to **`AGENTS.md`**.
